-se.da.Alan


// Interaction between two performers in real-time MIDI or Csound
// Open "-da.Beatrix" in another tab!
// Read https://bolprocessor.org/interactions-in-midi-and-csound/ for explanations


// This one works with real-time MIDI, but not with real-time Csound, because the notes need to be transferred, and Csound does not send them.

[Alan starts first and waits for Beatrix. His notes will be played by Beatrix.] 
_script(wait for E4 channel 1) {2, - F3 C#3 Eb3 A3 G#3 C3 Bb3 F#3 G3 B3 D3 E3}


// This one also works only with real-time MIDI

[Beatrix is waiting. Alan plays this and sends E0 with _transpose(12), i.e. E1 used to synchronise Beatrix. This note is inaudible because its velocity is 0] 
_transpose(12) _vel(60) E2 . D2 E2 . _vel(65) B2 D2 E2 . G2 B2 D2 E2 . _vel(70) F#2 G2 B2 D2 E2 . Bb2 F#2 G2 B2 D2 E2 . _vel(75) C2 Bb2 F#2 G2 B2 D2 E2 . _vel(77) G#2 C2 Bb2 F#2 G2 B2 D2 E2 . _vel(80) A2 G#2 C2 Bb2 F#2 G2 B2 D2 E2 . _vel(85) Eb2 A2 G#2 C2 Bb2 F#2 G2 B2 D2 E2 . _vel(87) C#2 Eb2 A2 G#2 C2 Bb2 F#2 G2 B2 D2 E2 . _vel(90) F2 C#2 Eb2 A2 G#2 C2 Bb2 F#2 G2 B2 D2 E2 _vel(0) E0 _script(wait for Stop)


// This one works both in real-time MIDI and Csound

[Beatrix started first and is waiting for the Start message. She will play her notes and send Continue so that Alan can play the following notes] 
E3 D3 C3 _script(MIDI send Start) _script(wait for Continue) A2 B2 C3 _script(MIDI send Stop)